<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Cappoint</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cappoint &lt;member&gt; &lt;position&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>cappoint fizban treasurer
</pre>
<p>Appoints a member of your clan to a position. The positions are:
</p>
<ul><li><b>treasurer</b>: they get access to the clan treasury (see <a cmd='#'>Help Cwithdraw</a>).</li>
<li><b>quartermaster</b>: they get access to the clan's equipment (see <a cmd='#'>Help Cunstore</a>).</li>
<li><b>lord</b>: only the clan Master can appoint a Lord. A Lord can take new members into the clan, among other things.</li>
<li><b>master</b>: only the clan Master can do this, and it hands the leadership of the clan over: the new Master takes your place, and you become an ordinary member.</li></ul>
<p>You can shorten the position, for example: cappoint fizban treas. You must 
be the clan Master, or have clan rank 25, to use cappoint; at rank 25 you 
can appoint treasurers and quartermasters only. The member must be in the 
game. To take a position away again, see <a cmd='#'>Help Cdepose</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Cdepose</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Cpromote</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Clan Commands</a>
</pre>




</div>